iety consisting of the amino acid sequence Tyr-Gly-Lys-Asp-Val-Lys-Asp-Leu-Phe-Asp-Tyr-Ala-Gln-Glu."],"label":"N-{beta-D-Man-(1-\u003e2)-beta-D-Man-(1-\u003e2)-beta-D-ManO[CH2]3S[CH2]2NHC(O)[CH2O]4C(O)[CH2]2S[CH2]2C(O)}-YGKDVKDLFDYAQE-NH-[CH2O]3[CH2]2C(O)NHC(CO2H)[CH2]4N3","obo_id":"CHEBI:141770","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["N-(1-{[beta-D-mannopyranosyl-(1-\u003e2)-beta-D-mannopyranosyl-(1-\u003e2)-beta-D-mannopyranosyl]oxy}-8,21,27-trioxo-11,14,17,20-tetraoxa-4,24-dithia-7-azaheptacosan-27-yl)-L-tyrosylglycyl-L-norleucyl-L-alpha-aspartyl-L-valyl-L-lysyl-L-alpha-aspartyl-L-leucyl-L-phenylalanyl-L-alpha-aspartyl-L-tyrosyl-L-alanyl-L-glutaminyl-N-[(14S)-18-azido-14-carboxy-12-oxo-3,6,9-trioxa-13-azaoctadecan-1-yl]-L-alpha-glutamine"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17277","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["UDP-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-D-glutamyl-L-lysyl-D-alanyl-D-alanine"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_17277","description":["UDP-glycopeptide having \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetylmuramoyl as the glyco portion and \u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-alanyl-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glutamyl-\u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-lysyl-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-alanyl-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-alanine as the peptide portion (attached via an amide bond between the amino terminus and the muramoyl carboxy group)."],"label":"UDP-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-gamma-D-glutamyl-L-lysyl-D-alanyl-D-alanine","obo_id":"CHEBI:17277","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_18199","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["UDP-Mur2Ac-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-A2pm-D-Ala-D-Ala","UDP-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-D-gamma-glutamyl-6-carboxy-L-lysyl-D-alanyl-D-alanine","UDP-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-D-glutamyl-6-carboxy-L-lysyl-D-alanyl-D-alanine","UDP-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-D-glutamyl-meso-2,6-diaminopimeloyl-D-alanyl-D-alanine"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_18199","description":["UDP-glycopeptide having \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetylmuramoyl as the glyco portion and \u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-alanyl-γ-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glutamyl-\u003ci\u003emeso\u003c/i\u003e-2,6-diaminopimeloyl-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-alanyl-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-alanine as the peptide portion (attached via an amide bond between the amino terminus and the muramoyl carboxy group)."],"label":"UDP-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-gamma-D-glutamyl-meso-2,6-diaminopimeloyl-D-alanyl-D-alanine","obo_id":"CHEBI:18199","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_22907","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Blenamax","Bleo","Bleocin","Bleomycin hexal","NSC-125066","bleomicina","bleomycine"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_22907","description":["A glycopeptide produced by the bacterium \u003cem\u003eStreptomyces verticillus\u003c/em\u003e. The term, \u0027bleomycin\u0027 refers to a family of structurally related compounds. When used as an anti-cancer agent, the chemotherapeutical forms are primarily bleomycin A\u003csmall\u003e\u003csub\u003e2\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/small\u003e and B\u003csmall\u003e\u003csub\u003e2\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/small\u003e."],"label":"bleomycin","obo_id":"CHEBI:22907","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_27877","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["N-Acetyl-D-glucosaminyl-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-Ala-D-glutamyl-6-carboxy-L-lysyl-D-alanine","beta-GlcNAc-(1-\u003e4)-MurNAc-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-6-carboxy-L-Lys-D-Ala"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_27877","description":["An \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetyl-β-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glycosaminyl glycopeptide consisting of an \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetyl-β-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glycosaminyl-(1→4)-\u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetylmuramoyl moiety attached to the amino terminus of the tetrapeptide \u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-alanyl-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glutamyl-6-carboxy-\u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-lysyl-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-alanine via an amide linkage."],"label":"N-acetyl-D-glucosaminyl-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-D-glutamyl-6-carboxy-L-lysyl-D-alanine","obo_id":"CHEBI:27877","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_28001","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["(1S,2R,18R,22S,25R,28R,40S)-22-(2-amino-2-oxoethyl)-48-[2-O-(3-amino-2,3,6-trideoxy-3-methyl-alpha-L-lyxo-hexopyranosyl)-beta-D-glucopyranosyloxy]-5,15-dichloro-2,18,32,35,37-pentahydroxy-19-[(N-methyl-D-leucyl)amino]-20,23,26,42,44-pentaoxo-7,13-dioxa-21,24,27,41,43-pentaazaoctacyclo[26.14.2.2(3,6).2(14,17).1(8,12).1(29,33).0(10,25).0(34,39)]pentaconta-3,5,8(48),9,11,14,16,29(45),30,32,34,36,38,46,49-pentadecaene-40-carboxylic acid","(2.2Sp,3.5Sa,2.6Sp)-O(4.2),C(3.4):C(5.4),O(4.6):C(3.5),C(2.7)-tricyclo[N-methyl-D-leucyl-3-chloro-(R)-beta-hydroxy-D-tyrosyl-L-asparaginyl-D-2-(4-{[2-O-(3-amino-2,3,6-trideoxy-3-C-methyl-alpha-L-lyxo-hexopyranosyl)-beta-D-glucopyranosyl]oxy}phenyl)glycyl-D-2-(4-hydroxyphenyl)glycyl-3-chloro-(R)-beta-hydroxy-L-tyrosyl-L-2-(3,5-dihydroxyphenyl)glycine]","(3S,6R,7R,11R,23S,26S,30aS,36R,38aR)-44-[2-O-(3-amino-2,3,6-trideoxy-3-C-methyl-alpha-L-lyxo-hexopyranosyl)-beta-D-glucopyranosyloxy]-3-(carbamoylmethyl)-10,19-dichloro-2,3,4,5,6,7,23,25,26,36,37,38,38a-tetradecahydro-7,22,28,30,32-pentahydroxy-6-(N-methyl-D-leucyl)-2,5,24,38,39-pentaoxo-1H,22H-23,36-(epiminomethano)-8,11:18,21-dietheno-13,16:31,35-di(metheno)[1,6,9]oxadiazacyclohexadecino[4,5-m][10,2,16]benzoxadiazacyclotetracosine-26-carboxylic acid","VANCOMYCIN","Vancocin","Vancomycin","vancomicin","vancomicina","vancomycin","vancomycine","vancomycinum"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_28001","description":["A complex glycopeptide from \u003cem\u003eStreptomyces orientalis\u003c/em\u003e. It inhibits a specific step in the synthesis of the peptidoglycan layer in the Gram-positive bacteria \u003cem\u003eStaphylococcus aureus\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem\u003eClostridium difficile\u003c/em\u003e."],"label":"vancomycin","obo_id":"CHEBI:28001","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["(3S,6R,7R,11R,23S,26S,30aS,36R,38aR)-44-[2-O-(3-amino-2,3,6-trideoxy-3-C-methyl-alpha-L-lyxo-hexopyranosyl)-beta-D-glucopyranosyloxy]-3-(carbamoylmethyl)-10,19-dichloro-2,3,4,5,6,7,23,25,26,36,37,38,38a-tetradecahydro-7,22,28,30,32-pentahydroxy-6-(N-methyl-D-leucyl)-2,5,24,38,39-pentaoxo-1H,22H-23,36-(epiminomethano)-8,11:18,21-dietheno-13,16:31,35-di(metheno)[1,6,9]oxadiazacyclohexadecino[4,5-m][10,2,16]benzoxadiazacyclotetracosine-26-carboxylic acid"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_28514","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["N-Acetyl-D-glucosaminyl-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-Ala-D-glutamyl-6-carboxy-L-lysine","beta-GlcNAc-(1-\u003e4)-MurNAc-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-6-carboxy-L-Lys"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_28514","description":["An \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetyl-β-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glycosaminyl glycopeptide consisting of an \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetyl-β-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glycosaminyl-(1→4)-\u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetylmuramoyl moiety attached to the amino terminus of the tripeptide \u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-alanyl-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glutamyl-6-carboxy-\u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-lysine via an amide linkage."],"label":"N-acetyl-D-glucosaminyl-(1-\u003e4)-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-D-glutamyl-6-carboxy-L-lysine","obo_id":"CHEBI:28514","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_29556","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Chloroorienticin A"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_29556","description":["A complex glycopeptide antibiotic that is isolated from \u003cem\u003eAmycolatopsis orientalis\u003c/em\u003e."],"label":"chloroeremomycin","obo_id":"CHEBI:29556","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_34994","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["teicoplanin A2-*"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_34994","description":["Any of the glycopeptides whose structure consists of teicoplanin A\u003csmall\u003e\u003csub\u003e3\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/small\u003e-1 in which the hydroxy group of the di(aryloxy)-substituted phenol moiety has been converted to the corresponding 2-acylamino-2-deoxy-β-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glucoside. Members of the class differ only in the nature of the acyl group."],"label":"teicoplanin A2","obo_id":"CHEBI:34994","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_34999","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["34-O-(2-(acetylamino)-2-deoxy-beta-D-glucopyranosyl)-22,31-dichloro-7-demethyl-64-O-demethyl-19-deoxy-42-O-alpha-D-mannopyranosylristomycin A aglycone","34-O-[2-(acetamido)-2-deoxy-beta-D-glucopyranosyl]-22,31-dichloro-7-demethyl-64-O-demethyl-19-deoxy-42-O-alpha-D-mannopyranosylristomycin A aglycone","Teicoplanin A3-1"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_34999","description":["A glycopeptide consisting of a macropolycyclic heptapeptide in which a phenolic hydroxy group has been converted to its α-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-mannoside while a secondary alcohol group has been converted to the corresponding 2-acetamido-2-deoxy-β-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glucoside."],"label":"teicoplanin A3-1","obo_id":"CHEBI:34999","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_47395","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["(1S,2R,18R,19R,22S,25R,28R,40S)-22-(2-amino-2-oxoethyl)-5,15-dichloro-2,18,32,35,37-pentahydroxy-19-{[(2R)-4-methyl-2-(methylamino)pentanoyl]amino}-20,23,26,42,44-pentaoxo-48-{[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)tetrahydro-2H-pyran-2-yl]oxy}-7,13-dioxa-21,24,27,41,43-pentaazaoctacyclo[26.14.2.2(3,6).2(14,17).1(8,12).1(29,33).0(10,25).0(34,39)]pentaconta-3,5,8(48),9,11,14,16,29(45),30,32,34,36,38,46,49-pentadecaene-40-carboxylic acid","Desvancosaminyl Vancomycin","pseudovancomycin","vancomycin pseudoaglycone"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_47395","description":["A glycopeptide that is vancomycin lacking the vancoaminyl residue."],"label":"devancoaminyl vancomycin","obo_id":"CHEBI:47395","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["(1S,2R,18R,19R,22S,25R,28R,40S)-22-(2-amino-2-oxoethyl)-5,15-dichloro-2,18,32,35,37-pentahydroxy-19-{[(2R)-4-methyl-2-(methylamino)pentanoyl]amino}-20,23,26,42,44-pentaoxo-48-{[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)tetrahydro-2H-pyran-2-yl]oxy}-7,13-dioxa-21,24,27,41,43-pentaazaoctacyclo[26.14.2.2(3,6).2(14,17).1(8,12).1(29,33).0(10,25).0(34,39)]pentaconta-3,5,8(48),9,11,14,16,29(45),30,32,34,36,38,46,49-pentadecaene-40-carboxylic acid"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_55424","ontology_name":"chebi","ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_55424","description":["An \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetyl-β-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glycosaminyl glycopeptide consisting of an \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetyl-β-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glycosaminyl-(1→4)-\u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetylmuramoyl moiety attached to the amino terminus of the pentapeptide \u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-Ala-γ-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-Glu-\u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-Lys-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-Ala-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-Ala via an amide linkage."],"label":"beta-GlcNAc-(1-\u003e4)-MurNAc-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-L-Lys-(D-Ala)2","obo_id":"CHEBI:55424","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_55478","ontology_name":"chebi","ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_55478","description":["An \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetyl-β-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glycosaminyl glycopeptide consisting of an \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetyl-β-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glycosaminyl-(1→4)-\u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetylmuramoyl moiety attached to the amino terminus of the pentapeptide \u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-Ala-γ-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-Glu-\u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e\u003csmall\u003e\u003csup\u003e6\u003c/small\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e-(β-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-Asp)-\u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-Lys-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-Ala-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-Ala via an amide linkage."],"label":"beta-GlcNAc-(1-\u003e4)-MurNAc-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-N(6)-(beta-D-Asp)-L-Lys-(D-Ala)2","obo_id":"CHEBI:55478","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_59315","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["GMDP","N-acetyl-(N-acetylglucosaminyl)muramoyl-L-alanyl-D-isoglutamine"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_59315","description":["An \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetyl-β-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glycosaminyl glycopeptide consisting of an \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetyl-β-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-glycosaminyl-(1→4)-\u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-acetylmuramoyl moiety attached to the amino terminus of the dipeptide \u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-alanyl-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-isoglutamine."],"label":"N-acetyl-4-(N-acetylglucosaminyl)muramoyl-L-alanyl-D-isoglutamine","obo_id":"CHEBI:59315","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_59414","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Acetylmuramyl-L-alanyl-D-isoglutamine","Acetylmuramyl-alanyl-isoglutamine","MDP","MurNAc-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu","N-acetylmuramyl-L-alanyl-D-isoglutamine","N2-(N-(N-Acetylmuramoyl)-L-alanyl)-D-alpha-glutamine"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_59414","description":["A glycopeptide that is \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-propionyl-\u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-alanyl-\u003csmall\u003eD\u003c/small\u003e-α-glutamine in which the pro-\u003ci\u003eR\u003c/i\u003e hydrogen of the propionyl group has been replaced by the oxygen at position 3 of