uence with an isostere-modified Ile-Ala-GlyΨ(CH\u003csmall\u003e\u003csub\u003e2\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/small\u003eCH\u003csmall\u003e\u003csub\u003e2\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/small\u003e)Phe tetrapeptoid unit attached to the amino terminus."],"label":"Ile-Ala-GlyPsi(CH2CH2)Phe-Lys(5-GalO)-Gly-Glu-Gln-Gly-Pro-Lys-Gly-Glu-Thr","obo_id":"CHEBI:63133","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["L-isoleucyl-L-alanyl-(2R,3E)-5-amino-2-benzylpentanoyl-(5R)-5-(beta-D-galactopyranosyloxy)-L-lysylglycyl-L-alpha-glutamyl-L-glutaminylglycyl-L-prolyl-L-lysylglycyl-L-alpha-glutamyl-L-threonine"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_63777","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["L4-MDP-ONB"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_63777","description":["A glycopeptide obtained by formal condensation of the carboxy group of 6-\u003cem\u003eO\u003c/em\u003e-butyrylated muramyl dipeptide with the hydroxy group of \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e-hydroxy-5-norbornene-2,3-dicarboxylmide."],"label":"6-O-butyryl-N-acetylmuramyl-L-alanyl-D-isoglutamine N-hydroxy-5-norbornene-2,3-dicarboxylmidyl ester","obo_id":"CHEBI:63777","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_64344","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["1-(2,4,6-trihydroxyphenyl)ethanone","2,4,6-trihydroxyacetophenone","2-acetylphloroglucinol","THAP","acetophloroglucine","acetylphloroglucinol","monoacetylphloroglucinol","phloracetophenone","phloroacetophenone"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_64344","description":["A benzenetriol that is acetophenone in which the hydrogens at positions 2, 4, and 6 on the phenyl group are replaced by hydroxy groups. It is used as a matrix in matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization (MALDI) mass spectrometry for the analysis of acidic glycans and glycopeptides."],"label":"2\u0027,4\u0027,6\u0027-trihydroxyacetophenone","obo_id":"CHEBI:64344","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["1-(2,4,6-trihydroxyphenyl)ethanone"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_67811","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Laramycin","U-30,604","U-30604","Zorbamycin"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_67811","description":["A  glycopeptide antibiotic found in \u003cem\u003eStreptomyces flavoviridis\u003c/em\u003e."],"label":"zorbamycin","obo_id":"CHEBI:67811","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_71229","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["N(3\u0027\u0027)-[2-(decylamino)ethyl]-29-{[(phosphonomethyl)amino]methyl}vancomycin","telavancin","telavancina","telavancine","telavancinum"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_71229","description":["A glycopeptide that is vancomycin substituted at position N-3\u0027\u0027 by a 2-(decylamino)ethyl group and at position C-29 by a (phosphonomethyl)aminomethyl group. Used as its hydrochloride salt for treatment of adults with complicated skin and skin structure infections caused by bacteria."],"label":"telavancin","obo_id":"CHEBI:71229","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_75044","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["phleomycins"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_75044","description":["A mixture of glycopeptide antibiotics originally isolated from the bacterium \u003cem\u003eStreptomyces verticillus\u003c/em\u003e whose components all contain a thiazolinylthiazole moiety and can form complexes with redox-active metals such as Co, Cu, and Fe. (Bleomycins are very similar to phleomycins, but have a bithiazole moiety in place of the thiazolinylthiazole moiety)."],"label":"phleomycin","obo_id":"CHEBI:75044","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_75046","ontology_name":"chebi","ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_75046","description":["A glycopeptide originally isolated from the bacterium \u003cem\u003eStreptomyces verticillus\u003c/em\u003e which contains a (4\u0027\u003ci\u003eR\u003c/i\u003e)-4\u0027,5\u0027-dihydro-2,4\u0027-bi-1,3-thiazole-2\u0027,4-diyl moiety with a a 4-guanidylbutylaminocarbonyl group attached to the 4-position of the terminal thiazole ring. Like all phleomycins, phleomycin D\u003csmall\u003e\u003csub\u003e1\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/small\u003e can form complexes with redox-active metals such as Co, Cu, and Fe."],"label":"phleomycin D1","obo_id":"CHEBI:75046","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_76058","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["(1S,2R,18R,19R,22S,25R,28R,40S)-2-{[(2R,4S,5R,6S)-4-amino-5-hydroxy-4,6-dimethyltetrahydro-2H-pyran-2-yl]oxy}-22-(2-amino-2-oxoethyl)-5,15-dichloro-18,32,35,37-tetrahydroxy-19-{[(2R)-4-methyl-2-(methylamino)pentanoyl]amino}-20,23,26,42,44-pentaoxo-48-{[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)tetrahydro-2H-pyran-2-yl]oxy}-7,13-dioxa-21,24,27,41,43-pentaazaoctacyclo[26.14.2.2(3,6).2(14,17).1(8,12).1(29,33).0(10,25).0(34,39)]pentaconta-3,5,8(48),9,11,14,16,29(45),30,32,34,36,38,46,49-pentadecaene-40-carboxylic acid"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_76058","description":["A glycopeptide that is isolated from \u003cem\u003eAmycolatopsis orientalis\u003c/em\u003e."],"label":"chloroorienticin B","obo_id":"CHEBI:76058","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["(1S,2R,18R,19R,22S,25R,28R,40S)-2-{[(2R,4S,5R,6S)-4-amino-5-hydroxy-4,6-dimethyltetrahydro-2H-pyran-2-yl]oxy}-22-(2-amino-2-oxoethyl)-5,15-dichloro-18,32,35,37-tetrahydroxy-19-{[(2R)-4-methyl-2-(methylamino)pentanoyl]amino}-20,23,26,42,44-pentaoxo-48-{[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)tetrahydro-2H-pyran-2-yl]oxy}-7,13-dioxa-21,24,27,41,43-pentaazaoctacyclo[26.14.2.2(3,6).2(14,17).1(8,12).1(29,33).0(10,25).0(34,39)]pentaconta-3,5,8(48),9,11,14,16,29(45),30,32,34,36,38,46,49-pentadecaene-40-carboxylic acid"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_82699","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["(4\u0027\u0027R)-22-O-(3-Amino-2,3,6-trideoxy-3-C-methyl-alpha-L-arabinohexopyranosyl)-N3\u0027\u0027-(p-(p-chlorophenyl)benzyl)vancomycin","(4\u0027\u0027R)-22-O-(3-